                        "glosses": [
                            "nie dający się rozdzielić, nie do podziału"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a43b6c84-b0b1-4fad-8d42-eaffbd238966",
                                "sense_id": "3286309e-4181-3218-8066-915e7b1e2ac1",
                                "text": "Czcimy nierozdzielną Trójcę."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f7c0bdde-57f8-4ef2-811f-bd1172fd6f9c",
                        "source_entry_id": "4789585b-f991-37f2-9a0b-d94f76e16f50",
                        "source_sense_id": "3286309e-4181-3218-8066-915e7b1e2ac1",
                        "target_lang_word": "inseparable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inseparable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd06e5e0-dc23-3095-8431-882bad0f0764",
                                        "entry_id": "c5129c67-1ec7-3bce-9129-cf023a0a84eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unable to be separated; bound together permanently."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e084cb35-027a-4f9a-9196-a6bcf747da63",
                                                "sense_id": "bd06e5e0-dc23-3095-8431-882bad0f0764",
                                                "text": "People of unalterable ideas still insisted upon calling him \"Sergeant\" when they met him, which was in some degree owing to his having still retained the well-shaped moustache of his military days, and the soldierly bearing inseparable from his form."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "847d2e1f-f96c-4ad5-920a-51b29cf47eac",
                                                "sense_id": "bd06e5e0-dc23-3095-8431-882bad0f0764",
                                                "text": "In the old days, to my commonplace and unobserving mind, he gave no evidences of genius whatsoever. He never read me any of his manuscripts, […] and therefore my lack of detection of his promise may in some degree be pardoned. But he had then none of the oddities and mannerisms which I hold to be inseparable from genius, and which struck my attention in after days when I came in contact with the Celebrity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6587697e-6835-47b3-9b26-b5c17200c241",
                                                "sense_id": "bd06e5e0-dc23-3095-8431-882bad0f0764",
                                                "text": "=This detail is one of the reasons which made a single, modern signalbox and the marshalling yard inseparable features in the modernisation of the Perth facilities. A central control point rather than 13 individual boxes, was essential to integrate with other movements the greatly increased flow of freight traffic through the station area."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "inseparable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e0df4b88-8429-3253-bf87-a419d9541800",
                                        "entry_id": "45bdb9c4-45a0-36f2-8ebe-4ba16dcecbca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that cannot be separated from something else."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "533c05bb-65ee-4822-9f11-a63796a19b89",
                                                "sense_id": "e0df4b88-8429-3253-bf87-a419d9541800",
                                                "text": "Jayanta does so in answering an opponent who declares that the very idea of a relation between two inseparables is self-contradictory. How can inseparability and relation be reconciled?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a57a2d86-e868-43b1-b9f1-bcc65495c991",
                        "source_entry_id": "4789585b-f991-37f2-9a0b-d94f76e16f50",
                        "source_sense_id": "3286309e-4181-3218-8066-915e7b1e2ac1",
                        "target_lang_word": "indissoluble",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "indissoluble",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
